[h1]Parley: The Negotiating Table[/h1]

[h1]At a glance[/h1]

[list]
[*]🟢 [b]Version 1.3.0[/b] · Targets CK3 [b]1.20.0.4[/b].
[*]🟢 [b]Standalone:[/b] no other mod required.
[*]🟢 [b]Negotiate marriage, money and allegiance in one treaty.[/b]
[*]🟢 [b]Languages:[/b] English, French, German, Japanese, Korean, Polish, Russian, Simplified Chinese, [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3090564070]來自無壹的中文翻譯[/url] and Spanish.
[*]🔴 [b]Changes gameplay:[/b] treaties can transfer money, people, land and vassalage.
[*]🔴 [b]WARNING — New rule: Negotiation interests.[/b] [b]Standard[/b] is the new-campaign default; unwanted payments lose value and wanted assets cost more to surrender. Choose [b]Off[/b] for the earlier valuation.
[*]🔴 [b]AGOT compatibility: awaiting the AGOT update for CK3 1.20.[/b]
[*]🔴 [b]Direct ruler negotiations only.[/b] Puppet proxy mode is unavailable.
[/list]

[h1]A wedding can win what a war cannot[/h1]

Negotiate marriage, money and allegiance with both sides and your counterpart's valuation visible.

[b]Auto-balance[/b] adjusts currencies toward [b]+1[/b] acceptance or reports it cannot.

AI envoys bring offers and demands: accept, negotiate or turn them away.

[h1]What you can negotiate[/h1]

[list]
[*][b]Payments:[/b] gold, with prestige and piety governed by game rules; influence when both governments support it.
[*][b]Marriage pacts:[/b] choose couples and marriage form, combine marriages, arrange eligible betrothals or promise a grand wedding.
[*][b]Land and allegiance:[/b] cede eligible titles, swear fealty with an editable contract, grant independence, or transfer eligible direct vassals.
[*][b]People and possessions:[/b] exchange artifacts, pledge relatives as hostages, or transfer eligible courtiers and accompanying families.
[*][b]Favors and pressure:[/b] promise or use a hook, or threaten a ruler with sufficient army, prestige and dread. Player and AI threats share the same minimum.
[/list]

Tooltips explain eligibility. Marriages can form alliances; alliances are not sold separately.

[h1]Reading the central panel[/h1]

[b]Their Answer[/b] combines benefits, costs, standing, demands and pressure from your partner's perspective.

With [b]Negotiation interests[/b] enabled, each term's percentage is a [b]valuation, not an acceptance chance[/b]:

[list]
[*][b]You offer:[/b] the partner's interest in receiving. A base 100-point term at 50% contributes 50 points.
[*][b]They offer:[/b] the partner's willingness to surrender. A base 100-point term at 50% costs 200 points.
[/list]

Higher percentages favor you in both directions. Rounded badges are red below [b]50%[/b], white at [b]50%[/b], green above it. Hover for components and selected base/adjusted points. Empty rows preview interest, not prices or trading permission.

The table shows [b]base points[/b]. [b]Interest[/b] deducts receiving discounts, surrender premiums and their effect on standing/bargaining once. Threats and called-in hooks remain separate pressure, without interest badges.

With interests enabled, ordinary agreements need an answer [b]above zero[/b]. Rounding affects display, not settlement. These are treaty points, not fixed gold prices.

[h1]Getting started[/h1]

[olist]
[*]Right-click an eligible landed ruler: [b]Diplomacy > Negotiate a Treaty[/b].
[*]Add terms in [b]You offer[/b] and [b]They offer[/b].
[*]Read [b]Their Answer[/b], adjust the package or use [b]Auto-balance[/b].
[*]Review and confirm. The mod rechecks that the agreement can be carried out.
[/olist]

🔴 [b]WARNING — Negotiation interests is new in 1.3.0:[/b] Off / Mild / [b]Standard (new-campaign default)[/b] / Strict. It changes valuations, not trading permissions or threat strength. Classic/Scaled base prices and currency restrictions remain separate. Gold, prestige and piety can each be selected on only one side. [url=https://github.com/G4VV4KH/-CK3-Parley-The-Negotiating-Table#game-rules-guide]Full rules, defaults and examples[/url].


When acting for a puppet, Parley's opener and marriage picker are hidden. Personal Rites determine marriage defaults and lineality pricing; native marriage eligibility checks still apply.

[h1]Compatibility and load order[/h1]

[b]Vanilla file replacements: none.[/b] Overhauls can still change treaty mechanics and need compatibility work.

[b]Optional vanilla load order:[/b]

[olist]
[*]Parley: The Negotiating Table
[*]Marriage Calculation Assistant
[/olist]

[b]AGOT is unsupported on CK3 1.20.[/b] Integration is disabled pending its update and checks. Both marriage assistants are optional, not general compatibility patches.

[b]Submods and companion mods:[/b]

[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3811100163]Marriage Calculation Assistant[/url]: marriage-candidate scores, breakdowns and sorting.
[*][url=https://github.com/G4VV4KH/-CK3-AGOT-Marriage-Calculation-Assistant]AGOT: Marriage Calculation Assistant[/url]: AGOT scoring for MCA; current compatibility is on hold.
[/list]

Enable one copy of each mod; no other patches are included.

[h1]Saves and known limits[/h1]

Before removal, use [b]Fold Away the Negotiating Table[/b] under [b]Mod Removal Decisions[/b], save, then disable Parley. This clears negotiation and AI state, but completed marriages, payments and transfers persist. Close MCA's picker before saving or removing MCA.

Title transfers exclude fealty/independence; overlapping courtier and hostage selections can invalidate a package.

With interests enabled, consequence previews for an already-refused manual offer are unavailable; refusal and retry remain possible.

Captions distinguish older [b]CK3 1.19.0.6[/b] screenshots from newer captures. [b]Multiplayer and long campaigns remain unverified.[/b]

[h1]Feedback and support[/h1]

For bugs, include versions, load order, UI scale, steps and a screenshot. Try reproducing with this family alone.

